module

# Verifies: SPEC §10 "a module holds only declarations (def / struct / enum / constants); top-level executable statements are forbidden"
# Decisions: DECISIONS.md D-DIAG-02 (E5002 = a top-level executable statement inside a module)
#
# print(...) is a top-level executable statement, and only declarations
# (def/struct/enum/constant) are allowed under a module directive, so this is E5002.
# By including only the executable statement and no declaration, this avoids
# incidental diagnostics such as an unused function (E4002).

print("module load side effect - forbidden by SPEC section 10")
